IoT = Internet of Things

It means connecting physical devices to the internet so they can collect, send, and sometimes act on data automatically.

Simple example
Smart AC

Sensor detects temperature.

Device sends data through the internet.

IoT system processes it.

AC automatically changes temperature.

Main components
Sensors → collect data (temperature, motion, distance, etc.)

Connectivity → Wi-Fi, Bluetooth, 4G/5G, etc.

Processing → analyzes the collected data

Cloud/Server → stores and manages data

Actuators → perform actions based on instructions

Examples
Smart home lights

Smart watches

Smart parking

Smart agriculture

Smart healthcare

Industrial monitoring

Arduino + ultrasonic sensor + buzzer is also a basic IoT-type system when connected to a network.
